# Optional: HTTP libraries and scraping frameworks that send their own name.
# They cannot solve the JavaScript challenge anyway, so refusing them saves
# one challenge page per request and keeps the outcome log readable.
#
# Do NOT include this for a decision that also covers an API or a feed that
# scripts are meant to use; turn the gate off for those locations instead.
# An empty User-Agent is listed last because map regexes match in order.

~*(scrapy|python-requests|python-urllib|aiohttp|httpx|go-http-client|okhttp)   deny;
~*(libwww-perl|lwp::simple|java/|apache-httpclient|node-fetch|axios|got\ \()   deny;
~*(headlesschrome|phantomjs|puppeteer|playwright|selenium)                     deny;
~^$                                                                            deny;
